{
	"_comment": "A switch's case values, as src/shared/switch-cases.ts reads them. `keys`: `caseKey` trims ASCII whitespace and lowers case, the one comparison a run, the duplicate check and the phone share. `choiceFields`: `choiceFieldOf` answers the field a subject names as exactly `event.<field>`, else null. `issues`: `switchIssues` over a switch's cases, with `choices` the subject's options or null when it names no choice field; each issue's `level`, `why` (empty, twice, vanished), `case`, and for a value its `chip` (place in its case) and `value`. `taken`: the case `caseTaken` answers each shown subject over the same cases and choices, the default past the last, a vanished value matching nothing; TypeScript only, since the phone never runs a switch. The phone's twin replays the rest.",
	"keys": [
		{ "value": "mention", "key": "mention" },
